## CODA startup
- '~/setcoda_2.5_brad' is a shell script that will set appropriate CODA environment
  variables for the FADC moller readout.  It is designed to be 'source'd by a start_coda
  script.  See next line.
- Start coda using by running the '~/start_coda_brad' script
  - it sources '~/setcoda_2.5_brad', then fires up the usual set of windows for ET, ER, EB, etc
  - the script ends with information on how to open the ROC console if you need it

## FlexIO board instead of TI board for interrupt generation
- The FlexIO board generates and interrupt on the OR of the two possible trigger types
  (Helicity Trigger and Data Trigger) and sends the ROC information on which triggers
  were present through an array structure.  The interrupt routine in the CRL can decide
  what to readout based on how the array vars are set (like a software IRQ handler).

## CRL compilation 
- The FADC crl must be compiled with a special makelist command located in
    /adaqfs/home/moller/crl/FADC/makelist.local
  Invoke it this way:
    ./makelist.local fadcmoller_list.crl ppc -mlongcall

## FADC HT trigger jumpers on backplane
- P2 (bottom-most backplane connector) needs two ECL jumpers installed to feed a copy
  of the HT trigger to the level converter board
  - Connect FADC slot pair (D22+, D23-) to SD-FP slot pair (D21+, D22-).  'D'
    is the right-most column on the P2 backplane connector.  The pins are
    numbered 1 to 32 (top to bottom).

## FADC HF (!MPS) input trigger min signal length
- Helicity Flip (!MPS) pulse needs to be at least 20 microsecs long or the
  FlexIO unit won't trigger on it correctly.
